rtation, and game roster, in conjunction with other coaching staff. Work closely with the Associate Director for Club Sports & Intramurals on the preparation of the season, schedule, and recruitment. Responsible for ongoing recruitment and retention of student-athletes. Manage coaching staff and student manager staff as hired by the Club Sports department. Foster strong, professional relationships with league representatives and officials, consistently demonstrating positive sportsmanship and conduct that reflects the University’s mission and values. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes A bachelor’s degree is preferred. 1-3 years of coaching experience at the high school, prep, junior, or collegiate level Must be willing and available to work nights and weekends, as the majority of games are Friday-Sunday Possess experience working with diverse staff, including college-age students Must maintain coaching certification or have the ability to acquire certification CPR/First Aid Certification Unusual Working Conditions Potential late nights due to practices and weekend availability for games or competitions. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff 